# Post-generation setup — <%= appName %>

This app was scaffolded with **create-mds-app**. Follow these steps to get it
running and ready to ship.

## 1. Install & run

```bash
yarn install          # or npm install / pnpm install
cp .env.example .env  # fill in values (see below)
yarn start            # Expo dev server (dev client)
```

The first native run requires generating the native projects:

```bash
npx expo prebuild     # creates ios/ and android/
yarn ios              # or: yarn android
```

> `ios/` and `android/` are git-ignored on purpose — they are regenerated from
> `app.config.ts` via prebuild. Keep configuration in `app.config.ts`, not in
> the native folders.

## 2. Environment variables

Edit `.env` (never commit it). Keys are inlined at build time, so **restart
Metro with `npx expo start --clear` after any change.**

| Variable | Required | Notes |
|----------|----------|-------|
| `EXPO_OWNER` | for EAS | Your Expo account/org username. |
| `EAS_PROJECT_ID` | for EAS | From `eas init` or the Expo dashboard. |
<% if (hasAuth) { -%>
| `EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL` | yes | Supabase project URL. |
| `EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_KEY` | yes | Supabase anon/publishable key. |
| `EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID` | for Google | Google OAuth web client id. |
<% } -%>
| `EXPO_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN` | optional | Enables crash reporting in production. |

## 3. EAS / OTA

The project is wired for EAS Build, Submit and OTA Updates (`eas.json`,
`app.config.ts`).

```bash
npm i -g eas-cli
eas login
eas init                       # links the project & sets the projectId
eas build --profile development --platform ios   # or android / all
```

OTA updates are **disabled for local `expo run:*`** and enabled only for the
`preview` and `production` build profiles (see `updates` in `app.config.ts`).

```bash
yarn update:preview            # push an OTA update to the preview channel
yarn update:production
```
